  "id": "DrugBank_DB00928 - MONDO_18433",
  "verbalization": "Azacitidine is implicated in the treatment of Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through a pathway involving Glasdegib, which is indicated for AML. The evidence suggests that Azacitidine may be repurposed for AML with the translocation T(6;9)(p23;q34), as it shares a common indication with Decitabine and Glasdegib. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, though not absolute, association between Azacitidine and the specific subtype of AML described. The mechanism appears to involve a shared therapeutic target, possibly through the action of Glasdegib, which is indicated for both AML and other related conditions. The integration of these pathways suggests that Azacitidine may exert its effects through a mechanism that is relevant to this particular subtype of AML, though the exact molecular pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
